      "writtenOn": "2025-09-29T14:50:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We return without calling prepare_switch_to_host(), so the caller will call __kvm_vcpu_enter_guest() again and then we will call prepare_switch_to_guest() again although we\u0027ve already switched to guest? Is this intended?\n\nEven if this is intended, it seems a bit unclean? Maybe it\u0027s better to call prepare_switch_to_guest() and prepare_switch_to_host() outside __kvm_vcpu_enter_guest()?",
      "revId": "79dcb2535ab20fb33e8a559419a6f957f48ca510",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bff87ad8_13788bf3",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/x86.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 3403,
      "author": {
        "id": 4085392
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-30T06:55:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003eIs this intended?\n\nYes. It is intended as `vmx-\u003eguest_uret_msrs_loaded` may be changed due to guest running, thus vmx_prepare_switch_to_guest() may need to run again. This is the same with the original code.\n\nNative KVM only has `prepare_switch_to_guest` ops, which will be called every time by `vcpu_enter_guest()` in the vcpu run loop. And it doesn\u0027t have `prepare_switch_to_host` ops as KVM-VMX code directly calls vmx_prepare_switch_to_host when put a vcpu (needed to load another vcpu, or back to user space, and so on).\n\nSo similarly to pkvm, we call `prepare_switch_to_guest` ops in the run loop, and call `prepare_switch_to_host` when switch back to the host.\n\n\u003eEven if this is intended, it seems a bit unclean? Maybe it\u0027s better to call prepare_switch_to_guest() and prepare_switch_to_host() outside __kvm_vcpu_enter_guest()?\n\nso calling `prepare_switch_to_host` ops to pair with `prepare_switch_to_guest` ops will do thing redundant as we only need to call `prepare_switch_to_host` ops once before exits from guest VM to host VM?",
      "parentUuid": "a0802d68_07e47113",
      "revId": "79dcb2535ab20fb33e8a559419a6f957f48ca510",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1f96ba2d_0e033665",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/x86.c",
